The FENIX package enables online checkpoint/restart with spare-rank replacement.

The package provides the following features:
* A kill command and fail fix, for injecting failures to test recovery
* A fenix command for enabling online recovery (i.e. without relaunching a job) using spare MPI ranks
* Optional in-memory checkpoints using Fenix's reliable memory-based checkpoint/restart functionality

The different options for the commands and fix are explained in the documentation.

This package currently requires building against the feature/cpp branch of Fenix (github.com/sandialabs/fenix).

Once built, you can test this package using one of the input files from the examples/PACKAGES/fenix dir. Input files must be passed with the "-in" flag, they cannot be sent through shell standard input.

